iMac 5K: never keep a root stream the disable pass already removed

amdgpu_dm_tiled_stitch_has_live_root_stream() lets the enable pass of
dm_update_crtc_state() accept a stitched-root modeset without reprogramming
("accept logical root modeset"). It judged the stream live from the old CRTC
state. But every flag that forces a modeset, mode_changed included, is settled
before the disable pass, and that pass removes such a CRTC's stream from the
DC context and clears it from the new state. Whenever the helper said yes, the
enable pass skipped the re-add with no stream left and hit
BUG_ON(dm_new_crtc_state->stream == NULL): an oops in the compositor's atomic
ioctl with the modeset locks held, which freezes the display for good.

Seen on iMac18,3, kernel 7.2.3, lean stack, 2026-09-10: after a pm_test
freezer cycle, Hyprland's first commit changed the HDR output metadata (none
to an SDR-EOTF blob), which amdgpu_dm_connector_atomic_check() turns into
mode_changed. Any such commit on the lit panel takes the same path: HDR
metadata on or off, or a colorspace or content-type change.

Require the new state to still hold the old stream. Because the removal always
comes first, such commits now take the full remove-and-add modeset that
mainline performs and every boot already exercises; the shortcut no longer
fires. Really keeping the stream would need the disable pass to skip the
removal under the same condition.

Applies on top of either stack: the helper is identical in both.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
@@ -297,10 +297,22 @@
 		const struct dm_crtc_state *dm_old_crtc_state,
 		const struct drm_crtc_state *new_crtc_state)
 {
+	const struct dm_crtc_state *dm_new_crtc_state =
+		container_of_const(new_crtc_state, struct dm_crtc_state, base);
+
 	if (!aconnector || !dm_old_crtc_state || !dm_old_crtc_state->stream ||
 	    !new_crtc_state->active || !new_crtc_state->mode_changed)
 		return false;
 
+	/*
+	 * The disable pass of this atomic check has already removed the stream
+	 * of every CRTC that needs a modeset and cleared it from the new state.
+	 * Only a stream the new state still holds can be kept: skipping the
+	 * re-add of a removed one reaches BUG_ON(!stream) after skip_modeset.
+	 */
+	if (dm_new_crtc_state->stream != dm_old_crtc_state->stream)
+		return false;
+
 	return amdgpu_dm_link_is_tiled_stitch_root(aconnector->dc_link) &&
 	       amdgpu_dm_link_is_tiled_stitch_root(dm_old_crtc_state->stream->link);
 }
